.Dd May 28, 2026
.Dt XTC_MCTX 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm xtc_mctx_create ,
.Nm xtc_mctx_destroy ,
.Nm xtc_mctx_alloc ,
.Nm xtc_mctx_calloc ,
.Nm xtc_mctx_strdup ,
.Nm xtc_mctx_free ,
.Nm xtc_mctx_register_cleanup ,
.Nm xtc_mctx_name ,
.Nm xtc_mctx_total_bytes ,
.Nm xtc_mctx_total_chunks ,
.Nm xtc_mctx_reset
.Nd hierarchical memory contexts with cleanup callbacks
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In xtc.h
.In xtc_mctx.h
.Ft int
.Fn xtc_mctx_create "xtc_mctx_t *parent" "const char *name" "xtc_mctx_t **out"
.Ft void
.Fn xtc_mctx_destroy "xtc_mctx_t *ctx"
.Ft "void *"
.Fn xtc_mctx_alloc "xtc_mctx_t *ctx" "size_t size"
.Ft "void *"
.Fn xtc_mctx_calloc "xtc_mctx_t *m" "size_t n" "size_t size"
.Ft "void *"
.Fn xtc_mctx_strdup "xtc_mctx_t *m" "const char *s"
.Ft void
.Fn xtc_mctx_free "xtc_mctx_t *m" "void *p"
.Ft int
.Fn xtc_mctx_register_cleanup "xtc_mctx_t *m" "xtc_mctx_cleanup_fn fn" "void *user"
.Ft "const char *"
.Fn xtc_mctx_name "const xtc_mctx_t *m"
.Ft size_t
.Fn xtc_mctx_total_bytes "const xtc_mctx_t *m"
.Ft size_t
.Fn xtc_mctx_total_chunks "const xtc_mctx_t *m"
.Ft void
.Fn xtc_mctx_reset "xtc_mctx_t *ctx"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm xtc_mctx
is a hierarchical memory context, modeled on PostgreSQL's
.Vt MemoryContext .
Allocations belong to a context; destroying the context bulk-frees
everything in it
.Pq plus all child contexts recursively .
Useful for request-scoped memory: create a context per request,
allocate freely, destroy at the end without tracking individual
frees.
.Pp
Each context can register cleanup callbacks fired on destroy
.Pq before the bulk-free
to release non-memory resources.
.Pp
.Fn xtc_mctx_alloc
returns raw memory within the context;
.Fn xtc_mctx_calloc
zeroes an
.Fa n
by
.Fa size
array; and
.Fn xtc_mctx_strdup
copies string
.Fa s
into the context.  All live until the context is reset or
destroyed.
.Fn xtc_mctx_free
optionally releases a single allocation early.
.Fn xtc_mctx_register_cleanup
adds a callback
.Fa fn
run in LIFO order at reset/destroy.
.Pp
.Fn xtc_mctx_name
returns the context's name;
.Fn xtc_mctx_total_bytes
and
.Fn xtc_mctx_total_chunks
report the memory and chunk count currently charged to the
context.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
xtc_mctx_t *root, *req;
xtc_mctx_create(NULL, "root", &root);
xtc_mctx_create(root, "request-42", &req);

/* Allocate request-scoped objects. */
char *buf = xtc_mctx_alloc(req, 4096);
struct widget *w = xtc_mctx_alloc(req, sizeof *w);

/* Done; bulk-free everything in req. */
xtc_mctx_destroy(req);
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr xtc_slab 3 ,
.Xr xtc_res 3 ,
.Xr xtc 7
.Sh HISTORY
Appeared in xtc 0.1.
